[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=SSH Interface Client v2.0\\\\Simpl# SSH client for 3-Series / 4-
  Cmn2=Series / VC-4. Drop-in replacement for\\the v1.7 processor with||1
  Cmn3=reconnect, host-key handling, and IP override\\moved into the Simpl#||1
  Cmn4=library.\\\\Use this module as a stand-alone SSH client. For inbound||1
  Cmn5=TCP on the\\processor, use the built-in SIMPL Windows TCP/IP Server||1
  Cmn6=symbol.\\\\-----------------------------------------------------
  Cmn7=---------------------------\\OPERATION\\------------------------
  Cmn8=--------------------------------------------------------\\Hold Connect||1
  Cmn9=high to connect. Release Connect to disconnect.\\Automatic retry||1
  Cmn10=after the remote SSH server is killed is not reliable yet\\(toggle||1
  Cmn11=Connect to recover).\\\\To_Server is sent as-is (no extra CR/LF).
  Cmn12=||1Size command strings in the\\program; From_Server is chunked at||1
  Cmn13=250 characters.\\\\IP_Address_Override, IP_Port_Override, Username_Override,||1
  Cmn14=and\\Password_Override$ replace the matching parameter when they||1
  Cmn15=have a\\value (port override must be greater than 0). Empty / 0||1
  Cmn16=reverts to the\\parameter. A change while Connect is held high reconnects.
  Cmn17=\\\\Host key:\\- Accept_Any_Key = Yes stores/trusts the first key||1
  Cmn18=automatically.\\- Accept_Any_Key = No raises Accept_New_Key_Notice||1
  Cmn19=and New_Key_Text$\\  when the fingerprint is unknown or has changed.
  Cmn20=||1Pulse Accept_New_Key\\  to store it and reconnect, or Decline_New_Key||1
  Cmn21=to abort.\\- Host keys are stored per symbol instance name:\\  \NVRAM\SSH_Interfa
  Cmn22=ce_v2_<GetSymbolInstanceName()>.key\\- Accept_Any_Key_Override high||1
  Cmn23=forces Accept_Any_Key = Yes for this\\  instance; low uses the Accept_Any_Key||1
  Cmn24=parameter.\\\\Connection_Status_Out:\\  1 Trying To Connect\\  2||1
  Cmn25=Connected\\  3 Not Connected\\  4 Non-Matching Fingerprint\\\\Do||1
  Cmn26=not bind IP_Port to 22 if this processor's own console SSH is in||1
  Cmn27=use\\on the same port of a remote device - 22 is correct for a normal||1
  Cmn28=SSH\\server (Cisco codec, Linux, etc.).\\\\---------------------
  Cmn29=-----------------------------------------------------------\\VERSION||1
  Cmn30=HISTORY\\-------------------------------------------------------
  Cmn31=-------------------------\\v2.0  8/21/2026  RGW\\  - New Simpl#||1
  Cmn32=core (SSH_Interface_v2.clz)\\  - Reconnect, host-key store, and||1
  Cmn33=TX gather live in Simpl#\\  - Password + keyboard-interactive authentication\\
  Cmn34=||2- IP override, unique ID, debug\\  - Inbound TCP: use SIMPL Windows||1
  Cmn35=TCP/IP Server (not this library)\\  - Debug is a digital input (hold||1
  Cmn36=high for console trace)\\  - Accept_Any_Key_Override digital; Unique_ID||1
  Cmn37=parameter removed\\    (host-key file uses GetSymbolInstanceName())
[END]
